Cfg [color: green, icon: settings, label: "config.py — P0 ✅ shipped · FIVE model pins (D-067, D-082)\nMODEL · USER_MODEL · LOOP_MODEL · NL_ASSERTION_MODEL · REVIEW_MODEL"]
NoOther [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-octagon, label: "ANTHROPIC ONLY — ollama and Cerebras are `doctor` diagnostics\nNEVER model sources · the quota REJECTS, so a wrong pin kills a run (D-067)"]

Gen > Adapter: REPLACED at the seam
Gen --> LiteLLM: what it used to call
Adapter > Sdk > Anthropic
Cfg > Adapter: which pin, per role
NoOther --> Cfg
Doctor [color: green, icon: activity, label: "doctor/ — P0, THE FIRST THING WRITTEN\n✅ shipped: `touchstone doctor` runs today · probes the AGENT pin by live call\nP1.0 adds the τ² data check · it checks NO trace server, because there is not one (D-077)\nfour modules by WHAT A CHECK NEEDS TO ANSWER — result, environment, pins, runtime — which is also their run order, so a failing environment check makes a runtime result a description of the wrong machine (D-102)"]
Doctor > Cfg

// ── 3 · the gates. Shadow earns enforce; nothing here carries a model in its verdict.
Gates3 [color: orange, icon: filter, label: "3 · the gates — D-064 · D-065\na gate is an EXTRACTED CONSTRAINT plus a MECHANICAL CHECK"] {
  Tier1 [color: orange, icon: hash, label: "gate/tier1.py — P2.1 ✅ shipped · ONE DB constraint, NO model\nD-105: retail tools.py already raises on 4 of D-064 five — 0 firings on 506 accepted calls\nself_swap is the one nothing checks — policy.md:132\nsilent on the corpus: 0 accepted firings in 1,712; all 37 sit in tasks D-080 excluded\nD-064 2.1% recall was nablo + cloudsurf-4B — a different population, rule 12"]
  Tier2 [color: orange, icon: cpu, label: "gate/predicate.py + gate/extract.py — P2.2 ✅ shipped\nthe model TRANSLATES a stated constraint into a predicate. The VERDICT is mechanical. It never judges 'did well'\nD-106: three shapes — RequiresPriorTool, RequiresUserAssent, ArgumentIn. Data, never model-authored Python\nshapes measured first: cancel reason 0 firings, authentication 1 in 1,824, confirmation 83\nDEF-076: 44 of the 934 clean sessions fire confirmation, 23 corroborated — the control set is not clean\nD-107: extract.py is the third module allowed to reach a model — it PROPOSES, predicate.py decides\nloop/budget.py reads the SDK quota; the curator runs tools=[] allowed_tools=[] setting_sources=[]"]
  Shadow [color: orange, icon: eye, label: "SHADOW — P2.3 · judges a COMPLETED session, acts on nothing\na gate earns enforcement here, or it does not get it"]
  Enforce [color: pink, icon: shield, label: "gate/enforce.py — P3.1 · REFUSES the call before it executes\nthe hook at make_tool_call()"]
}

Tier1 > Shadow
Tier2 > Shadow
Shadow > Enforce: ONLY with a measured precision and recall (D-065)
Enforce > EnvCall: refuse — before the write happens
Precision [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "PERFECT PRECISION, 2.1% RECALL on a strong agent\nthe low recall is the FEATURE — only a gate that never fires falsely can be enforced"]
Precision --> Tier1
Headroom [shape: document, color: orange, icon: target, label: "tier 2 targets the 26 FLAKY tasks — where the headroom is\n⚠ its false-positive rate on the 85 always-passing tasks is what shadow measures"]
Headroom --> Tier2

// ── 4 · what an attempt lands on. One status, plus an orthogonal flag.
Ends [color: red, icon: flag, label: "4 · exactly ONE status per attempt — docs/09 §6"] {
  Scored [color: green, icon: check-circle, label: "scored — counts toward everything"]
  ParseFail [color: red, icon: x-circle, label: "parse_failure — scored WRONG\nnever retried (D-013)"]
  Voided [color: grey, icon: slash, label: "void — rate limit, or model changed\ncounts toward NOTHING (D-015)"]
  Incomplete [color: grey, icon: pause-circle, label: "incomplete — process died\nthe five-hour window is the realistic cause"]
}
Orch > Ends: every attempt lands on exactly one
BudgetFlag [shape: document, color: red, icon: dollar-sign, label: "budget_exceeded — a FLAG, never a status\nlands BESIDE any of the four, NEVER instead of one"]
Orch > BudgetFlag: orthogonal to where the attempt lands

// ── 5 · telemetry. This is the edge D-063 got wrong, and the picture says so.
TelemetryPy [color: blue, icon: activity, label: "5 · telemetry.py — P1.2 ✅ shipped\ntouchstone.* — NEVER gen_ai.* (D-017)\nthe span is opened by adapter.py ITSELF (D-073) — no instrumentor can emit it\nmlflow.start_span, NOT the OTel SDK — D-074 deleted it and the first cut of the seam used it anyway\nD-096: NO provider and NO exporter — the row said otherwise and described the pre-D-074 stack"]
D063 [shape: document, color: purple, icon: help-circle, label: "D-063 assumed litellm's OTel callback\nP1.1 ✅ shipped and killed it — generate() is replaced whole, so litellm never runs for these roles"]
D063 --> TelemetryPy
Adapter > TelemetryPy: one span per model call, all four roles
EnvCall > TelemetryPy: one span per tool call, and per REFUSAL
