Stores [color: blue, icon: hard-drive, label: "6 · what survives the process"] {
  Spans [shape: cylinder, icon: file-text, label: "results/spans/(version).jsonl\nthe scorer's ONLY input"]
  Bench [shape: document, color: blue, icon: lock, label: "suite/benchmark/manifest.json — P1.3 ✅ shipped · task IDS and a hash\nNEVER task bytes — vendoring makes us the corpus's owner again\nthe 10 are a numeric-sorted PREFIX of τ²'s OWN held-out test split, not a sample and not hand-picked (D-098)\ncollation is pinned WITH the hash — the ids are decimal strings, so string sort is a different ten tasks"]
}
TelemetryPy > Spans
Bench > Orch: which tasks — the ids only

// ── 7 · the driver and the scorer.
CliPy [color: blue, icon: terminal, label: "cli.py — P0 shipped `doctor`\nP1.6 ✅ adds run · score — TWO of the three the row names\nsuite is NOT deferred here: the row went stale, all five of its verbs were deferred AFTER it was written and every one reads a regression tier that phase 3 creates (D-103)\nscore takes a VERSION, never a --results path — an arbitrary file would publish τ²'s four third-party baselines under one of our version labels, which D-080 ceiling 1 forbids\nevery command imports what it drives INSIDE the function, so doctor never pays τ²'s 1.71s to say the machine is broken"]
RunPy [color: blue, icon: play, label: "loop/run.py — P1.6 ✅ shipped · k attempts, config.K = 3 (D-030)\nTHIN: run_domain is τ²'s. Ours is the three things it cannot do — install the adapter, restrict to the frozen ten, and REFUSE a run the adapter did not attach to (D-103)\ninstall() returning under 2 raises: a run that quiet succeeds, measures litellm and reports it as ours\n--resume is τ²'s OWN auto_resume, not a cache we built — D-015 was already climbed upstream, checked before building\noutput lands in τ²'s data dir under touchstone-(version), namespaced because four shipped baselines live in that tree"]
ReportPy [color: blue, icon: file-text, label: "loop/report.py — P1.6 ✅ shipped · the ENVELOPE around what score() computed (D-103)\nprovenance read from the file that wrote it, never restated: benchmark_hash and tau2_commit from the manifest, model from the run\nNOT info.git_commit — τ² stamps that with the commit of whatever directory it was launched from, which is OURS (DEF-074)\nwrite() refuses a results file whose task ids are not the frozen ten: benchmark_hash is a claim nothing downstream can contradict\nspan-derived keys stay ABSENT, not zero — a key emitted as 0 before anything measures it is a published number nothing computed"]
CliPy > Doctor: the P0 subcommand — implemented since P0 and the only one that has ever been EXECUTED; run and score ship at P1.6 but wait on quota
CliPy > RunPy > Orch

Scoring [color: blue, icon: bar-chart-2, label: "7 · scoring — P1.5"] {
  ScorePy [color: blue, icon: bar-chart-2, label: "loop/score.py — NO model call (D-007)\nspans + reward_breakdown → results/(version).json\npass^k is the HEADLINE · pass@1 beside it — BOTH, especially when they differ\nP1.5 ✅ shipped · COPIES upstream pass^k and is_successful, never imports them — 1.56s against a 2s suite gate (D-099)\ndoctor re-checks the copy against the pin over every trials<=5 grid point; the plausible re-derivation agrees only where k = trials\ninfra errors count as FAILED — the leaderboard convention, the OPPOSITE of tau2 get_metrics_df, and the file says which\nthe payload is FOUR TypedDicts, not dict[str, Any] and not pydantic — nothing crosses a trust boundary here (D-100)\nthose four live in loop/schema.py, NOT here — doctor and the score command read them too, and a shape three callers share inside one of them makes the other two import a step to reach a type (D-102)\nall ten termination reasons are the TypedDict's OWN keys, so omitting one is a type error — but a MISSPELT one passes mypy and every test, and only doctor's diff against the upstream enum catches it"]
  Diag [shape: document, color: red, icon: eye-off, label: "diagnostics{} — inside results/(version).json\ncompare.py NEVER reads inside it — ONE TEST proves it (D-045)\nNO OUTGOING EDGE, ON PURPOSE"]
  Judge [color: orange, icon: award, label: "the ROUTER rubric — LOOP_MODEL (D-082)\nit SELECTS which traces enter the loop and CANNOT GATE\ncriterion_1_agreement over all 1,712 is its MEASURED error rate"]
}
Spans > ScorePy
Reward > ScorePy: the answer key, and it is τ²'s, not ours
ScorePy > ReportPy: aggregate + cases — the two halves score() can fill alone
RunPy > ReportPy: the τ² results file, and the ids it must match
ScorePy > Diag: the OTHER output — and it stops here
Judge > Diag: writes the rubric fields — and reaches NOTHING else
DeepEval [color: grey, icon: bar-chart-2, label: "deepeval — an OPTIONAL extra, `diagnostics` · D-076\nnothing that gates may import it · telemetry opted out at import"]
DeepEval > Diag: trajectory diagnostics — and, like the judge, reaches NOTHING else
Shadow --> Diag: the shadow scores land here until a gate earns enforcement

// ── 8 · decision 2. Five conditions, all mechanical.
Cmp [color: grey, icon: filter, label: "8 · loop/compare.py — P2.4 · DEFERRED, D-080 · NOTHING HERE RUNS\nspecified in full because this is what it revives to — it has no SECOND OPERAND until a second version exists"] {
  C1 [icon: hash, label: "1 · benchmark_hash(C) == benchmark_hash(I)"]
  C2 [color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "2 · NO per-task regression — THE ONE THAT WORKS\nfires on pass^k → not-pass^k ONLY (D-008)"]
  C3 [icon: trending-up, label: "3 · strict improvement on ≥ 1 metric\nelse a no-op is accepted"]
  C4 [icon: dollar-sign, label: "4 · no budget breach — cost per success, p95"]
  C5 [color: grey, icon: lock, label: "5 · no locked task fails — ONE-WAY\nopen/locked is DELETED, not vacuous — it locks on an ACCEPTED version and there are none (D-080)"]
}
C1 > C2 > C3 > C4 > C5
ScorePy > Cmp: results/(version).json — the scored half only
Accepted [shape: oval, color: green, icon: check, label: "ACCEPT — vN is the champion"]
Refused [shape: oval, color: red, icon: x, label: "REJECT — the rejection IS the result\nNEVER fixed by weakening the baseline"]
C5 > Accepted: all five hold
Cmp > Refused: any ONE fails

// ── 8a · THE FEED (D-080). The inner loop needed a failing trace and a control set, and
//  that was the ONLY thing the outer loop owed it — so it is fed from τ²'s own shipped runs
//  instead. ⚠ SELECTION IS NOT GATING, and reusing one number for both was the defect.
//  reward_breakdown[DB] compares FINAL DATABASE STATE and is blind to how the state was
//  reached: an agent that skips a required confirmation and still writes the correct row
//  scores DB == 1. Feeding on DB == 0 alone left 371 such traces in the SILENCE SET, where
//  a CORRECT predicate would have been rejected as a false positive.
//
//  🔴 D-082 §A DEMOTED THIS WHOLE SECTION AND THE PICTURE DID NOT FOLLOW FOR A DAY.
//  The router REPLACED "the mechanical select" — D-082's own table says so in the row that
//  retires `analyst` + `select` + the unbuilt rubric judge into one agent. But 8a went on
//  drawing `select` as a DIAMOND feeding the loop, and 8b's router went on reading "drawn
//  from the 834", so the two sections together said the mechanical selector still selects
//  and the router runs after it. ⛔ NEITHER SECTION WAS WRONG ALONE, AND THE STALE TOPOLOGY
//  SAT ON THE BOUNDARY BETWEEN THEM — which is the place no single section's review looks.
//  a7fc003 rewired every edge INSIDE 8b (the critic got its own hand-back; the five gauntlet
//  gates collapsed to three) and touched not one edge INTO it: Corpus still fed the diamond,
//  and the diamond still fed the router. ⚠ THE FIRST WRITE-UP OF THIS SAID a7fc003 "touched
//  no EDGE", which is FALSE — `git show a7fc003 -- diagrams/touchstone.eraser` has TWELVE
//  changed edge lines, five removed and seven added. Caught on the pass that wrote DEF-060,
//  by re-reading the diff instead of the sentence about it. Rule 10, on a paragraph about
//  rule 10 — and the corrected sentence's own number was wrong on its first draft too.
//
//  WHAT THE THREE SIGNALS ARE NOW: the ANSWER KEY. They are free — τ²'s own evaluator
//  already computed them and they sit in the shipped result JSONs — so they cost nothing to
//  keep, and D-082 §B spends them on `criterion_1_agreement`: the router's verdict scored
//  against a population whose answer is already known. ⛔ NO RESULT IS REPORTABLE WITHOUT IT.
//  ⚠ AND THE CLEAN 878 IS STILL THE SILENCE SET. That is D-080 and D-082 did not touch it.
//  ⚠ THE SKIP EDGE IS THE EXPENSIVE HALF OF §A, AND IT IS DRAWN ON PURPOSE. A router `skip`
//  lands in the control set, so a MODEL now helps define the population a gate must be silent
//  on — "silent on the clean traces" degrades to "silent on the traces a model called clean",
//  gate and population sharing one failure mode. D-082 §B is the price paid for it, which is
//  why the Cal node hangs off the router and not off the corpus.
Feed [color: pink, icon: filter, label: "8a · the feed — D-080 · τ²'s OWN shipped runs, never a run of ours"] {
  Corpus [color: grey, icon: archive, label: "1,712 simulations τ²-bench SHIPS — data/tau2/results/final/\n107 of 114 tasks — the 7 whose gold actions moved are EXCLUDED, not repaired"]
  Signals [shape: document, color: grey, icon: key, label: "τ²'s OWN signals — the UNION of THREE, and since D-082 §B the ANSWER KEY rather than the selector\n⚠ NOT reward_breakdown[DB] == 0 alone · free: already in the shipped result JSONs"]
  Anom [color: orange, icon: alert-circle, label: "834 ANOMALOUS\n407 the DB check failed · +371 DB PASSED and an action_check failed · +56 a WRITE nobody confirmed"]
  Clean [color: green, icon: check-circle, label: "THE CONTROL SET — 878 clean by τ²'s three signals, PLUS every session the router SKIPPED (D-082 §A)\na gate that fires here is a FALSE POSITIVE · ⚠ the 878 is mechanical, the skips are not — which is what Cal exists to price\n⚠ 7 of the 878 are task 105, clean because its ONLY gold action raises and evaluator_env.py swallows it — DEF-075\nKEPT, not removed: 878 is a published denominator and 0.8% cannot move a verdict — D-104 §C"]
}
Corpus > Signals
Signals > Anom
Signals > Clean
SelNotGate [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "SELECTION IS NOT GATING — D-080\nDB stays the GATE's metric because it is mechanical, and it is a POOR SELECTOR for the same reason — it cannot see process\n⚠ the 56 is an UPPER BOUND from a regex over the last user message before each WRITE — enough to widen the selector, NOT a figure to quote"]
SelNotGate --> Signals

// ── 8b · THE INNER LOOP (D-070). Every other stage on this page runs ONCE per
//  candidate version. This one runs up to n times on a SINGLE failing trace, and it
//  is the only mechanism here that makes the measurement grow rather than report it.
//  The model sits in TRANSLATE and nowhere else — the verdict at TEST is a predicate
//  evaluation, which is the invariant of section 9 applied to the loop that feeds it.
//  ⚠ THE SCOPE FILTER USED TO STAND HERE AND IT IS DELETED — D-081, DEF-056. A diamond
//  asked "does this break a rule someone WROTE DOWN?" and routed a `no` to a second
//  terminal. It was called MECHANICAL in docs/02-gates.md and it named no file, no
//  predicate and no model. ⛔ IT COULD NOT HAVE BEEN MECHANICAL: a mechanical answer to
//  "was a stated rule broken?" IS the predicate translate produces, so the filter wanted
//  the loop's output as its own input. run_predicate() was always the only filter that
//  defended anything — a candidate that fires on the clean set is rejected whatever a
//  scope check believed. ⚠ WHAT IT COST TO DELETE: up to n model calls on a trace with no
//  rule to find. Unpaid today, and the exhaustion records ARE the measurement of it.
//  ⚠ The phase-3 exit gate still requires one recorded UNMINEABLE and now gets a BETTER
//  one — every attempt and its counterexample, not a bare assertion that no rule
//  existed.
Mine [color: pink, icon: refresh-cw, label: "8b · mine — P3.4 · THE INNER LOOP, and a second LangGraph graph (D-071) · up to config.MAX_ATTEMPTS attempts on ONE failing trace\nthe CRITIC decides (D-086) and run_predicate is EVIDENCE, not a gate — the scope filter is DELETED (D-081) · the outer loop REPORTS a number; this loop makes the number COVER MORE"] {
  M0 [shape: diamond, color: pink, icon: alert-circle, label: "1 · ROUTER — rubric, D-082 §A · reads ONE τ² session and returns ENHANCE or SKIP\nit is THE SELECTOR now — it replaced `analyst`, the mechanical `select` and the unbuilt rubric judge"]
  MT [color: orange, icon: cpu, label: "2 · CURATOR — decides WHETHER a failure is worth an eval at all, names the rule it broke, writes the predicate\nD-086 C · the loop's centre of gravity. It proposes a CANDIDATE; it never CLEARS one"]
  MCrit [color: orange, icon: eye, label: "3 · CRITIC / QA — the ONLY judge of the curator's call, and the loop's DECISION POINT · D-086 A\nit runs the predicate, reads the result, and picks: bounce, hand over, or give up\nit exists because D-040 admitted the hole: a rule can be reproducible, distinct and still measure nothing interesting"]
  MTest [shape: diamond, color: orange, icon: check-square, label: "4 · run_predicate() — mechanical, no model. EVIDENCE, not a gate — D-086 A overturned D-081's 'only decision point'\nfires on the TARGET session? must be YES\nfires on ANY of the 878 CLEAN? must be NO"]
  MBudget [icon: edit-3, color: green, label: "attempt_budget() — the critic's OTHER tool, D-089\nnamed for the job and not the consequence — a name saying only 'record' invites a second owner of the cap, D-092\nowns config.MAX_ATTEMPTS: says EXIT, records a give-up, may REFUSE\n⚠ ONE function reads the cap and the graph's edge calls the same one — D-091\ntwo places that know the cap are two places that can disagree about it\nflags go to the MLflow span for a human; the loop does NOT branch on them — D-090 D"]
  MEdge [icon: alert-triangle, color: red, label: "FORCE-TERMINATE — the conditional edge, D-094\nfires ONLY when an agent is told to exit and continues anyway\ncalls attempts_exhausted(), the same function the tool calls — D-091\nexit_reason force_terminated, expected value 0\nan alarm and not a category: the safety net stays BECAUSE it should never fire"]
  MGive [shape: oval, color: grey, icon: x-circle, label: "UNMINEABLE\nevery attempt and its counterexample recorded\n⚠ a RESULT, not an error — and not retried forever"]
}
M0 > MT: ENHANCE — straight to the curator. There is no pre-check, and never was one that worked
PosMem > MT: D-087 — the curator checks its candidate against the CLEARED suite. Exact half runs the cleared predicates on the trace BEFORE any agent call; the suite index goes in the prompt. Still no tool
M0 > Clean: SKIP — a skipped session joins the CONTROL SET. D-082 §A
MT > MCrit: the candidate goes to QA
MCrit > MT: hand-back — the SPECIFIC bad finding, never 'this seems weak'. D-086 C: a vague objection costs an attempt and teaches nothing. ONE bounce per attempt (D-082)
MCrit > MTest: the critic calls its ONE tool — D-085 gave it, D-086 A kept it. No other node calls run_predicate
MTest > MCrit: the result returns to its CALLER, who DECIDES what it means — D-086 A. There is NO run_predicate > curator edge
MCrit > MBudget: may I keep going? — and giving up goes through the same tool; every UNMINEABLE has >=1 run_predicate result behind it (D-082, D-086 A, D-089)
MBudget > MGive: its reply IS the exit — everything is already recorded, nothing hands off (D-094 A); exit_reason rides on the record (D-093 B)
MBudget > MEdge: an agent was told to exit and kept going anyway
MEdge > MGive: force_terminated — expected value 0, and non-zero is a bug report against a prompt (D-094 C)
Corpus > M0: one session at a time — ALL 1,712, because the router is what selects now
Clean > MTest: the silence set — the NO half of the evidence
Cal [shape: document, color: red, icon: percent, label: "criterion_1_agreement — the router's verdict against τ²'s own signals, over all 1,712\nD-082 §B · NO RESULT IS REPORTABLE WITHOUT IT — a router verdict with no agreement figure is a population with no provenance\n⚠ if it comes back poor, §A REVERTS: the rubric becomes a diagnostic and selection goes back to mechanical"]
Cal --> M0
Anom --> Cal: the 834 the signals flagged
Clean --> Cal: and the 878 they did not — together, the answer already known
Overfit [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "SILENT ON THE PASSING SET IS A CLAIM ABOUT THE SESSIONS THAT RAN\nnever about the domain — and the SLOWER CONTROL that used to cover it is GONE\n⚠ a case arrived `open` and gated only once an ACCEPTED version was quiet on it — D-080 deleted that, so a cleared predicate rests ENTIRELY on this corpus"]
Overfit --> MTest

// ── 8c · THE CURATOR'S TWO MEMORIES (D-078), and the first thing to say is which memory
//  this is NOT. It is not the agent's. The agent's memory is FROZEN and reset per attempt,
//  because it is the thing being measured; this one GROWS, because it is loop plumbing.
//  ⛔ NEITHER IS A MEMORY LIBRARY, A VECTOR STORE, OR CONVERSATION HISTORY. D-022 and D-027
//     are unchanged and this decision does not reopen them.
//  ⚠ THE ASYMMETRY IS THE DESIGN. Positive memory is EXACT because a predicate either fires
//    or it does not — you query it by running it, so it cannot drift from what it claims.
//    Negative memory is a HEURISTIC view and says so: Igor (CCS'21) measured stack-hash
//    bucketing over-counting distinct crashes by 1–2 orders of magnitude and under-counting
//    coverage by 2–3. A negative signature is the same shape of guess, so it is DERIVED and
//    never stored — a `sig_version` bump rebuilds every bucket rather than migrating it.
Curator [color: pink, icon: database, label: "8c · the curator's TWO memories — P3.4 · D-078\nNOT the agent's memory — that one is FROZEN and reset per attempt, because it is what is measured"] {
  PosMem [color: green, icon: check-square, label: "positive — THE ACTIVE RULE SET, queried by RUNNING it\nexact, because a predicate either fires or it does not"]
  NegMem [color: grey, icon: x-square, label: "negative — a RECOMPUTABLE VIEW over retained failing traces\nheuristic, derived-never-stored · a sig_version bump rebuilds it, never migrates it"]
}
Gauntlet --> PosMem: a cleared rule IS the positive memory
MGive --> NegMem: every UNMINEABLE lands here, with its counterexamples
NegMem --> M0: has this shape already been dealt with? — prevalence ranking, D-078 · D-081 rewired this from the deleted filter

// ── 8d · WITHDRAWN 2026-08-21, AND THE WITHDRAWAL IS THE ENTRY. A `Human` node stood here
//  for one day carrying "D-079 part 3 · the HUMAN REMEDY", with edges from MSkip and Refused.
//  ⛔ IT WAS NEVER DECIDED. On 2026-08-20 the instruction was "I have suggested to change only
//     human in loop (discard it)", and on 2026-08-21 the follow-up was "I never said" about the
//     gate-blocks-and-a-human-fixes-it framing being attributed back. The one supporting remark —
//     "some human will definetly update the prompt/policy/rules" — was made inside a hypothesis
//     prefaced "This is just an thought, we aren't planning to run retail agents."
//  🔴 THE MECHANISM IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING. A correction arrived naming TWO things; one half
//     was applied and the other half was not re-derived. That is rule 10 — a correction is the
//     highest-error, lowest-re-reading edit in the file — and it produced a NODE, not a sentence.
//  ⛔ A REMARK INSIDE A HYPOTHESIS THE SPEAKER HAS ALREADY DISCLAIMED IS NOT A DECISION.
//     Grade it U, or do not draw it. An invented reason collapses on "what else did you consider?"
//  ✅ WHAT SURVIVES D-079 is below, and it is the half nobody disputed: evals are the forcing
//     function, and the STANDARD they measure against does not move. MGive is a plain
//     terminal now — it RECORDS, which is all the phase-3 exit gate ever asked of it. (MSkip stood
//     beside it until D-081 deleted the scope filter; MGive is the only terminal left.)
Immutable [shape: document, color: red, icon: lock, label: "THE STANDARD DOES NOT MOVE — D-079\nthe retail policy document is ground truth the gate derives from · the agent's prompt, rules and tools are the lever\na gate made green by editing the standard is 'the test failed so I changed the test'"]
Immutable --> MT

// ── 9 · the three decisions, side by side. None of them may contain a model.
Decisions [color: red, icon: git-branch, label: "9 · THREE decisions — and 'promotion' named only the middle one"] {
  D1 [icon: shield, label: "1 · refuse a TOOL CALL — runtime, P3.1\nno model in the verdict"]
  D2 [icon: filter, label: "2 · reject a CANDIDATE VERSION — at compare, P2.4\nno model in the verdict"]
  D3 [icon: filter, label: "3 · clear a MINED CASE — at suite gauntlet, P3.5\nno model in the verdict · fed by the inner loop, section 8b"]
}
Enforce > D1
Cmp > D2
Invariant [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-octagon, label: "ANYTHING THAT GATES IS MECHANICAL\nANYTHING WITH A MODEL IN IT CANNOT GATE\nD-064 puts the model in TRANSLATION, never in the VERDICT"]
Invariant --> Decisions

Gauntlet [color: green, icon: filter, label: "10 · THE GAUNTLET — renamed from `admission` by D-088, because one act was the wrong shape for three independent gates\nthe gauntlet's three gates — P3.5, all mechanical. No human is a step, and no AGENT is either: three boolean checks, no model\nD-084 dropped not_a_void and merged not_flaky · D-086 D: the ONLY mechanical boundary left. BACKLOG, not deferred — it runs on a FINISHED candidate, so the loop has to exist before its input does"] {
