NoInherit [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "v1 WAS TO BE MEASURED HERE, NEVER INHERITED — and it is SUPERSEDED, D-080\nits output was a corpus of traces to mine, and one already ships · ⚠ τ²'s four baselines stay CONTEXT, never a reference line\n⚠ what is genuinely gone with it: haiku's simulator-fabrication rate, which nobody else can measure for us"]
NoInherit --> V1

// ── 11b · THE AGENT GRAPH (D-071 part A). Four nodes, and the whole design is one
//  constraint: EVERY MUTATION IS CONFINED TO ONE NODE. That is not tidiness — it is what
//  gives gate/enforce.py exactly one caller to attribute a refusal to. With writes fanned
//  across three specialists a refusal is attributable to no node, and the P3 exit gate
//  ("a REFUSED tool call is in a committed trace") stops meaning anything.
//  ⚠ `policy` having no τ² tool at all is the second half: a node with no domain tool is a
//  reasoning node BY CONSTRUCTION, not by instruction. It cannot quietly become an actor.
//  ⛔ THIS IS v5 AND ONLY v5. v1 through v4 run τ²'s stock LLMAgent — we own no prompt
//     before P3.6, which is exactly why the gates are measured against someone else's agent.
AgentGraph [color: grey, icon: git-branch, label: "11b · agent/ — OUR retail agent — P3.6 · v5 · D-071 · DEFERRED with the ladder, D-080 — designed, not built\na LangGraph graph, NOT the SDK's subagents — the SDK's graph is not versionable"] {
  Sup [color: pink, icon: repeat, label: "supervisor — routes, and routes only"]
  NIdent [icon: user, label: "identity — who is this, what did they buy?\nfour READ tools"]
  NCat [icon: package, label: "catalogue — what is this item, what could replace it?\nthree READ tools + calculate, which upstream types GENERIC — not READ"]
  NPol [color: orange, icon: book, label: "policy — what does the policy permit HERE?\nno τ² tool at all — reads the policy doc over our MCP server"]
  NSyn [color: red, icon: edit-3, label: "synthesizer — commit it\nTHE ONLY NODE THAT MAY CALL A WRITE TOOL · the 7 WRITEs + transfer_to_human_agents"]
}
Sup > NIdent
Sup > NCat
Sup > NPol
Sup > NSyn
NSyn > EnvCall: every mutation in v5 leaves through here, and only here
V5 --> AgentGraph: the rung this graph IS
OneWriter [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-octagon, label: "ONE WRITING NODE IS THE LOAD-BEARING PART\nit gives the enforcement point exactly ONE caller to attribute a refusal to"]
